<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  feature:dsh-workspace intentionally declares no permission, provider, service or activity.

  * INTERNET and the app-wide `usesCleartextTraffic` flag belong to app/AndroidManifest.xml and
    already admit the loopback http://127.0.0.1:<port> DSH origin.
  * Uploads use the Storage Access Framework (ACTION_GET_CONTENT / ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT) and
    downloads use DownloadManager's public Downloads destination on API 29+ or the app-specific
    external files directory on API 26-28, so no storage permission is required.
  * The WebView requests camera/microphone only through WebChromeClient.onPermissionRequest; the
    module denies them because no dangerous permission is declared. Adding one is an app-level
    decision (see README.md), never something this library does on its own.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" />
